                <item>
                <title><![CDATA[【Albums (lossy)】MP3 - Madonna - Confessions II - The Film (Audio) [MP3 320kbps]]]></title>
                <link><![CDATA[https://sharemania.us/threads/madonna-confessions-ii-the-film-audio-mp3-320kbps.301477/]]></link>
                <description><![CDATA[<article>
				<blockquote class="messageText SelectQuoteContainer ugc baseHtml">
					
					<div style="text-align: center"><img src="https://iili.io/CfI2fKg.png" class="bbCodeImage LbImage" alt="[​IMG]" data-url="https://iili.io/CfI2fKg.png" style=""><br>
<br>
<b>Madonna - Confessions II - The Film (Audio) [MP3 320kbps] </b><br>
<br>
The album's accompanying <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Musical_film" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">musical film</a>, <i>Confessions II – The Film</i>, built around the first six songs, was directed by TORSO (David Toro and Solomon Chase). It stars Madonna, with appearances by <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arca_(musician)" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Arca</a>, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Archie_Madekwe" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Archie Madekwe</a>, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Benedict_Cumberbatch" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Benedict Cumberbatch</a>, Carpenter, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cole_Palmer" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Cole Palmer</a>, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Debi_Mazar" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Debi Mazar</a>, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gwendoline_Christie" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Gwendoline Christie</a>, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Honey_Dijon" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Honey Dijon</a>, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Feid" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Feid</a>, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jo%C3%A3o_Pedro_(footballer,_born_2001)" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">João Pedro</a>, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Julia_Garner" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Julia Garner</a>, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kate_Moss" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Kate Moss</a>, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Odessa_A%27zion" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Odessa A'zion</a>, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Richard_E._Grant" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Richard E. Grant</a>, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shygirl" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Shygirl</a>, and <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lourdes_Leon" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Lourdes Leon</a>. The film premiered on June 5, 2026, at the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beacon_Theatre_(New_York_City)" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Beacon Theatre</a> in <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_York_City" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">New York City</a>, during the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tribeca_Festival" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Tribeca Festival</a>, followed by Madonna's conversation with <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anderson_Cooper" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Anderson Cooper</a> filling in for the initially announced moderator <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jimmy_Fallon" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Jimmy Fallon</a>. It was released on <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/YouTube" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">YouTube</a> on June 8, 2026.<br>
<br>
